Module boundaries expose only names marked with `$export` in the appropriate facade.

### Shared helpers

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    -- components/utils.moth
    internal_value #= 42
]

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    -- components/@mod.moth
    $export
    @utils internal_value
]

A parent module may now bind `@components internal_value`. It cannot bypass the child facade with `@components/utils`.

### Separate root scopes

Declarations authored in `@mod.moth`, `@package.moth` or `@entry.moth` remain local to that root. Shared code belongs in ordinary helper files.

`@mod.moth` publishes the normal API and `@package.moth` publishes the support API. `@entry.moth` publishes none. Resolution never falls back from one facade to another.

See @#module-visibility (Module visibility) and @#project-local-packages (Project-local packages).
